prakṛtyā niyatāḥ svayā\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":2261,\"bb\":2004,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/20/b2004/\",\"shadow_value\":\"kāmaiḥ – by desires; taiḥ taiḥ – various; hṛta – deprived of; jñānāḥ – knowledge; prapadyante – surrender; anya – to other; devatāḥ – demigods; tam tam – corresponding; niyamam – regulations; āsthāya – following; prakṛtyā – by nature; niyatāḥ – controlled; svayā – by their own.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"kāmaiḥ\",\"translation\":\"by desires\"},{\"word\":\"taiḥ taiḥ\",\"translation\":\"various\"},{\"word\":\"hṛta\",\"translation\":\"deprived of\"},{\"word\":\"jñānāḥ\",\"translation\":\"knowledge\"},{\"word\":\"prapadyante\",\"translation\":\"surrender\"},{\"word\":\"anya\",\"translation\":\"to other\"},{\"word\":\"devatāḥ\",\"translation\":\"demigods\"},{\"word\":\"tam tam\",\"translation\":\"corresponding\"},{\"word\":\"niyamam\",\"translation\":\"regulations\"},{\"word\":\"āsthāya\",\"translation\":\"following\"},{\"word\":\"prakṛtyā\",\"translation\":\"by nature\"},{\"word\":\"niyatāḥ\",\"translation\":\"controlled\"},{\"word\":\"svayā\",\"translation\":\"by their own\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":2262,\"bb\":2005,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/20/b2005/\",\"body_value\":\"Those whose intelligence has been stolen by material desires surrender unto demigods and follow the particular rules and regulations of worship according to their own natures.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2263,\"bb\":2006,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/20/b2006/\",\"body_value\":\"Those who are freed from all material contaminations surrender unto the Supreme Lord and engage in His devotional service. As long as the material contamination is not completely washed off, they are by nature nondevotees. But even those who have material desires and who resort to the Supreme Lord are not so much attracted by external nature; because of approaching the right goal, they soon become free from all material lust. In the Śrīmad-Bhāgavatam it is recommended that whether one is a pure devotee and is free from all material desires, or is full of material desires, or desires liberation from material contamination, he should in all cases surrender to Vāsudeva and worship Him. As stated in the Bhāgavatam (2.3.10):\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":2264,\"bb\":2007,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/20/b2007/\",\"body_value\":\"akāmaḥ sarva-kāmo vā
mokṣa-kāma udāra-dhīḥ
tīvreṇa bhakti-yogena
yajeta puruṣaṁ param\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2265,\"bb\":2008,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/20/b2008/\",\"body_value\":\"$25\"}]}],\"short_title\":\"Bg. 7.20\",\"medium_title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is 7.20\"},\"locale\":\"en\",\"activeView\":\"$6:props:activeView\"}]}],\"$L26\",\"$L27\",\"$L28\"]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"2a:I[83068,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n30:I[78455,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n26:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-4 w-full max-w-screen-xl mx-auto md:px-8 mb-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"nav\",null,{\"aria-label\":\"Breadcrumb\",\"className\":\"breadcrumb mb-8 text-base\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"/en/library/\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L20\",null,{\"href\":\"/en/library/\",\"className\":\"text-vb-link\",\"children\":\"Library\"}],\" » \"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"/en/library/bg/\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L20\",null,{\"href\":\"/en/library/bg/\",\"className\":\"text-vb-link\",\"children\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is\"}],\" » \"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"/en/library/bg/7/\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L20\",null,{\"href\":\"/en/library/bg/7/\",\"className\":\"text-vb-link\",\"children\"